{# How to change a plan tree with the plan tools. One call writes the whole tree, so the
   node ids and the version come from the newest plan result. The person approves a plan on
   the page, and no tool does. #}
Changing a research plan tree

1. Call {{ tool('read_plan') }} first. It gives each node with its number path, such as 2 or 2.1, and the version of the tree.
2. Each top-level node is a section. The nodes under it are its tasks, in their order.
3. To change the tree, call {{ tool('write_plan') }} with the version and the whole tree below the root. Give each node its `text` and its `children`.
4. To keep a node, give its `node_id` or its number path from the newest plan result. A node with no `node_id` is new. A node that you leave out is removed.
5. To move a node, put it under its new parent in the tree that you send. To rename it, send its `node_id` with the new text.
6. The text of a node is one line of at most 120 characters. A plan holds at most 4 sections and 150 nodes. The root text does not change.

A refused call with `stale_version` returns the current tree and writes nothing. Read that tree, and send the whole tree again with its version.

The person approves the plan on the page. After the approval, the plan runs, and the tools cannot change it. A refused call that names an executing plan means that the plan runs already. Do not send that call again.
